license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DanielMartin-Arogyasami/criterialogic"
abstract: >-
  Evaluation toolkit and data for LLM reasoning over clinical-trial eligibility
  criteria. A real-criteria arm uses criteria segmented verbatim from a dated
  ClinicalTrials.gov snapshot, with each mapped form checked against its source
  sentence. A compositional arm composes predicates from the same snapshot into
  nested AND/OR/NOT expressions labelled by a three-valued evaluator, in designs
  that vary nesting depth and expression size separately. Released with the
  snapshot, the atom pool, the item sets, per-item predictions, the
  reasoning-failure codebook and both annotators' labels.
keywords:
  - clinical trial eligibility
  - patient-trial matching
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - logical reasoning
  - clinical NLP
  - calibration
